EDITION: news-paper concept where the typography is what moves

The three previous attempts each failed on the opposite axis: one was
deliberately frozen, one was glowing glass cards (rejected as "glossy / AI
slop"), one was flat with no motion (rejected as "worse"). The brief this time
was explicit: full animation, tidy, clean, should look like news.

That combination set the constraint, and the constraint produced the concept:
what moves is TYPE, not light. Orbs, glow and glass are out; the moving
vocabulary is paper — words get typeset, rules get drawn, blocks get wiped in,
numbers count up, a two-row ticker counter-scrolls.

Measured: 48 elements animate on load/enter, 7 headline words with 7 distinct
stagger delays, 15 of 17 rules draw from scaleX 0, ticker 42s vs 74s
counter-directional, counters land exactly on their real values, and only 3
elements loop forever (ticker + live dot).

Structure is a newspaper: dateline masthead, lead story with a standing dek
column and fact block, secondary stories in tight 1px-grid columns whose rules
turn red on hover, a ledger table, sticky case-study rail, drop caps.
Three type roles (Newsreader / IBM Plex Sans / IBM Plex Mono).

All eight anti-slop gates still demand ZERO and are proven failable by
injecting one instance of every tell into the running page.

Three defects only measurement caught:
1. Glued words with JS disabled - innerText read "Softwarethatgetsused,not
   justshipped." because the space sat inside the clipped span. Spaces are now
   text nodes outside the spans. The no-JS gate exists precisely because full
   animation can leave a page empty when it goes wrong.
2. Motion that could not be measured because it had already finished - the
   first gate waited for networkidle plus 1.2s and then reported "no motion"
   while the motion was real. The recorder now attaches before load and
   samples every frame.
3. Ticker contrast failed in BOTH themes (2.40:1 in light). No single accent
   value is safe on --ink, so a --accent-on-ink token flips between themes.

52 gates green locally and against the live origin: 39 edition + 13 perf.
